          "name": "guard_the_gate_plan.txt",
          "contents": "*** MY PLAN: ***\n\nMy secret passwords:\n- \n- \n\nCondition for \"no password was given,\" in words:\n\n\nCondition, written in Python:\n\n\nWhat I'll print once a valid password is given:\n\n\n*** MY TESTING: ***\n\nPredict what will happen for each scenario BEFORE you run your program.\nThen run it and record what actually happened.\n\nScenario               | Inputs I'll type, in order | Predicted behavior | Actual behavior\n------------------------|------------------------------|----------------------|------------------\nExits immediately       |                              |                      |\nLoops once, then exits  |                              |                      |\nLoops twice, then exits |                              |                      |\n                         |                              |                      |\n                         |                              |                      |\n\nChoose your own scenarios for the last two rows — try a blank input, a sneaky\ninput, or something that tests your challenge rule.\n\n\n*** MY PARTNER TEST: ***\n\nMy attempt to trick my partner's guardian:\n\n\nDid I get past it, or did their loop catch me?\n\n\nIf I got past it, what might they change?\n\n\n*** MY REFLECTION: ***\n\nIf you used AI Tutor to help, reflect below on how you used it and how you used its output.\n\n\nHow did testing go? Did you update any part of your program as a result? Explain.",
